            <ArticleTitle>One-pot synthesis of multicomponent (Mo, Co) metal sulfide/carbon nanoboxes as anode materials for improving Na-ion storage.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>10820-10823</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc06192g</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Multicomponent MoS2/Co9S8/C hollow nanocubes were developed by the one-pot solvothermal method and a subsequent calcination process. Benefitting from the merits of hollow structures, the highly-conductive carbon matrix and the buffering effect provided by uniformly-mixed MoS2 and Co9S8, the MoS2/Co9S8/C anode shows high capacity and rate capability as the anode of sodium-ion batteries.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
